Hello,

I am am after some interpretation on how the RN model works and how the below results are possible? I have created a simple model to attempt to compare the abundance and detection probability values between four different models of camera. For each camera model I can obtain different abundance estimates, but using the same predict() method the detection probability estimates are exactly the same for all cameras. How is it possible that I can obtain different abundance estimates when detection probability is the same for all cameras? What have I done wrong, I must be calculating detection probability wrong?

sample code below:

#load data
> cat <- read.csv("Cat.detection.history.pilot.s1.csv",header=TRUE)

#create unmarkedFrame
> y <- cat[,2:8]
> siteCovs <- cat[,c("camera"),drop=FALSE]
> pilot <- unmarkedFrameOccu(y=y,siteCovs=siteCovs)

#Create model
> m1 <- occuRN(~1 ~camera, pilot)
