hi Mathilde,
 yes the elements of the matrix are the counts of birds or frogs or whatever you sampled.   So that matrix shows that 0 birds were observed at site 1, primary period 1, and for both secondary periods.

  If you have the data in that format, such as in a spreadsheet, then you would have to read the data into R and use the unmarkedFramePCO function to package it up in a format suitable for use by unmarked functions (as in the help file and examples).

regards
andy

